rota lap 5343, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; read up close and run the actual thing, so the lap RAN tools/fixtures/r/rank_outcome_scan.sh over the elder ranked page rather than reasoning about how the ranking went
think Absence check first: grep found tools/fixtures/r/rank_outcome_scan.sh and its witness already standing, so the instrument I was about to propose exists and takes --page. The lap became writing rather than building.
think Ran the scan on the elder page. Two readings that point opposite ways -- Kendall tau 0.9556 over 45 pairs says the ranking predicted the read order almost exactly, and falsifier_faulted 10 of 12 says the falsifier half failed. The claim half is the easy half, measured rather than suspected.
think That reading names the discipline the second page inherits: every row states the reading that would fire its falsifier, as a command or an instrument this tree already owns, and a row without one is declined.
think Subject followed the elder's own measurements rather than my preference. The torus rows fell -- fold clustered nothing, the privilege radius over-admitted 48 conferrals, a 2x2 torus and mesh are one graph -- and the bound and refusal rows stood. So the nine draw from the surviving half.
think Nine rows rather than twelve, because three further rows I sketched had no reachable reading for their falsifiers and the page's own discipline declines those.
obs The new page is gradeable by the existing instrument on arrival -- rank_outcome_scan.sh --page reads ranked_rows=9, rows_without_erratum=9 -- so no new instrument was built and no claim was owed.
obs I copied the bearing-quorum scan's path out of the elder's own erratum under an m letter room, and no such file has ever existed; it lives under b. A broken citation in a design page propagates, because the next page quotes it rather than running it.
obs That fault is invisible to backtick_path by law: the guard classes a dated basename as testimony, and every active-designing page carries one. Measured over 234 living pages -- 46 broken tool citations across 30, of which 37 resolve by basename and 9 are absent everywhere, each lawfully. No red; the resolvers and accrete-never-break cover every case.
obs The card's own copy of that illustration DID red backtick_path at living=66 against a ceiling of 65, exactly copal's firing three hours earlier. Depathed to plain words and the guard returned to 65, green.
obs A 31-minute stale hot roster pass held the run lock with a launch_head no longer HEAD; verified its cwd was this tree before TERMing it, per the runner's own instruction.
